WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.007
Codeville.

00:00:01.007 --> 00:00:02.341
Built for vibe coders.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.824
This is the real Codeville app.

00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:09.589
It checks Git, Claude Code and Node, then you open your project.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.727
An analysis agent reads it:

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:18.240
the stack, the layers, every feature, and how they connect.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.596
Your prompts, made visual.

00:00:24.596 --> 00:00:27.807
Each feature is a district, and every file is a block.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.244
Pick a file, and the town shows where it lives.

00:00:33.244 --> 00:00:34.789
Open it right in the editor.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.783
Links show how the parts talk to each other.

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:45.451
Now, just prompt.

00:00:45.451 --> 00:00:47.939
Ask Claude Code for a wishlist feature...

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:57.743
and watch every file it writes land in your project, live, with its tests.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.712
Run the tests, and a shopper walks every case.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:16.282
It stops at the broken one, and tells you what to fix next.

00:01:20.107 --> 00:01:21.518
So ask Claude to fix it.

00:01:21.518 --> 00:01:22.752
All eight tests pass.

00:01:31.307 --> 00:01:32.061
Then ship it.

00:01:32.061 --> 00:01:34.208
Stage, commit and push, in one click.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.159
And the fun part.

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:48.650
Turn on your camera, and your code becomes a hologram, like Tony Stark's lab.

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:55.235
Move your open hand to turn it.

00:01:55.235 --> 00:01:59.575
Spread two hands to zoom, make a fist to hold, and pinch twice to reset.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:10.083
Codeville.

00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:10.736
Vibe code.

00:02:10.736 --> 00:02:11.585
See it build.
